{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7367b6ec7ad16ba2","name":"card_event_hell_on_wheels","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BloodIron/events/card_event_hell_on_wheels","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HELL ON WHEELS","text":"Duplicate a friendly tank and reduce its operation cost by 2. Double its attack if a Sherman.","flavorText":"The 2nd Armored Division was a US armored division during WWII. The division earned its nickname \"Hell on Wheels\" from General George S. Patton during training maneuvers in the United States in the early 1940s. Patton, who was known for his colorful language and larger-than-life personality, was impressed by the division speed, aggressiveness and mobility in mock combat exercises. He remarked that they moved like “hell on wheels,” a phrase that stuck and became the division’s official nickname. The division's first major action came during Operation Torch in 1942, where it fought alongside Allied forces to push the Axis troops out of French North Africa. Following the success in North Africa, Hell on Wheels participated in the invasion of Sicily in 1943 and later the D-Day landings on Omaha Beach on June 6th, 1944. The division advanced through France and Belgium, where it participated in the Battle of the Bulge, and crossed the Rhine River into Germany. After the war the division remained stationed in Germany as part of the Allied occupation forces, before returning to the United States in 1946.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_hell_on_wheels","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hell_on_wheels_title","SourceString":"HELL ON WHEELS","LocalizedString":"HELL ON WHEELS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hell_on_wheels_text","SourceString":"Duplicate a friendly tank and reduce its operation cost by 2. Double its attack if a Sherman.","LocalizedString":"Duplicate a friendly tank and reduce its operation cost by 2. Double its attack if a Sherman."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hell_on_wheels_history","SourceString":"The 2nd Armored Division was a US armored division during WWII. The division earned its nickname \"Hell on Wheels\" from General George S. Patton during training maneuvers in the United States in the early 1940s. Patton, who was known for his colorful language and larger-than-life personality, was impressed by the division speed, aggressiveness and mobility in mock combat exercises. He remarked that they moved like “hell on wheels,” a phrase that stuck and became the division’s official nickname. The division's first major action came during Operation Torch in 1942, where it fought alongside Allied forces to push the Axis troops out of French North Africa. Following the success in North Africa, Hell on Wheels participated in the invasion of Sicily in 1943 and later the D-Day landings on Omaha Beach on June 6th, 1944. The division advanced through France and Belgium, where it participated in the Battle of the Bulge, and crossed the Rhine River into Germany. After the war the division remained stationed in Germany as part of the Allied occupation forces, before returning to the United States in 1946.","LocalizedString":"The 2nd Armored Division was a US armored division during WWII. The division earned its nickname \"Hell on Wheels\" from General George S. Patton during training maneuvers in the United States in the early 1940s. Patton, who was known for his colorful language and larger-than-life personality, was impressed by the division speed, aggressiveness and mobility in mock combat exercises. He remarked that they moved like “hell on wheels,” a phrase that stuck and became the division’s official nickname. The division's first major action came during Operation Torch in 1942, where it fought alongside Allied forces to push the Axis troops out of French North Africa. Following the success in North Africa, Hell on Wheels participated in the invasion of Sicily in 1943 and later the D-Day landings on Omaha Beach on June 6th, 1944. The division advanced through France and Belgium, where it participated in the Battle of the Bulge, and crossed the Rhine River into Germany. After the war the division remained stationed in Germany as part of the Allied occupation forces, before returning to the United States in 1946."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Tank_Medium_Move_Fx'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Tank_Medium_Move_Fx.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/Winter_2024/t_us_elite_order_2.t_us_elite_order_2","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/HELL_ON_WHEELS.HELL_ON_WHEELS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":395.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hell_on_wheels_photo","SourceString":"Infantry and tanks of the 2nd Armored Division during the Battle of the Bulge, December 1944.","LocalizedString":"Infantry and tanks of the 2nd Armored Division during the Battle of the Bulge, December 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isAttackBuff":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tmpTarget","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_hell_on_wheels_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pur